'''British Baliscans''' are [[Baliscans|Baliscan]] residents with fully or partial [[W:Antecedent (genealogy)|antecedents]] from the [[United Kingdom]]. The British have been very important in the development of the Baliscan identity, especially since the 1705 [[W:Pact of Genoa|Pact of Genoa]]. They include Baliscans of [[W:English people|English]], [[W:Scottish people|Scottish]], [[W:Ulster Scots people|Ulster Scots]], (Northern) [[W:Irish people|Irish]] and [[W:Welsh people|Welsh]] ancestry. The numbers of Scottish and Welsh are highest in [[Cerdanya]] (specifically in the [[Cadaqués]] and [[Dríadas]] regions).

Beginning in the post-confederation years, British industrialists and landowners had outsized economic influence in Cerdanya, pioneering the development of the first Baliscan railroads, while others migrated as railway engineers, civil engineers and to work in banking and commerce (after the [[Ivorran Gold Rush]]). 

